module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.emitted_entry_point_succeeds_doing_nothing

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data emitted_entry_point_succeeds_doing_nothing: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "emitted_entry_point_succeeds_doing_nothing" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an emitted entry point that succeeds having done nothing** (a code generator, asked for an artifact whose source declares no runnable entry, writes a well-formed entry point with an EMPTY BODY rather than saying so, so the artifact builds, runs, exits zero and performs none of the program's work). ",

    "INVALID STATE: the emitter reaches an arm selected by an ABSENCE -- no declared entry function and no pipeline module -- and renders a syntactically valid empty entry instead of a refusal, then reports the emission as complete. ",

    "HARM: fabricated plausible output in DESIGN section 5's sense, which is OUTSIDE the guarantee ladder rather than low on it -- a clean exit is read as the emitted program having worked, and no reader can distinguish it from one that ran. ",

    "The compounding harm is countability: silence joins to nothing, so the gap appears in no census and never ranks for closing, which is how this one survived under a self-hosting program whose section 7 obligation is proof BY EXECUTION at exactly that point. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the tell is an absence-selected arm whose body is a valid-but-empty construct rather than a diagnostic, sitting beside a SIBLING ARM IN THE SAME EMITTER that refuses the analogous absence properly. ",

    "When the fail-closed shape is authorable twenty lines away, the fabricating arm is an inconsistency and not a limitation. ",

    "WHY IT IS NOT refusal_deferred_to_emitted_runtime: the discriminator is whose inability is hidden. ",

    "There the compiler KNEW it could not answer a DECLARED fact and wrote that knowledge into the artifact instead of the diagnostic stream; here nothing was declared, and a refusing artifact is truthfully reporting a property of its own source. ",

    "SPECIMEN AND HOW IT WAS FOUND: v1.compiler.emit_rust emit_main_rs rendered an empty-body main for every corpus with no workflow function and no v1.compiler.compile module, while the same function's has_pipeline arm rendered emit_candidate_cli_host, which refuses per verb with a located message and exit 2. ",

    "Found by READING THE EMITTER after a measurement was generalised from one entry's closure into a claim about emission: the measurement said main was empty, and only the emitter said which predicate made it so. ",

    "REPAIR: v1.compiler.emit_rust emit_entry_point_absent_main_rs, whose refusal names which of the two absences held and exits 2, with the marker held as one authority read by both the emitter and the receipt. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: for every generator arm selected by an absence, ask what the produced artifact DOES when someone runs it. ",

    "If the answer is 'succeeds', the arm belongs to this class regardless of how honest the surrounding code reads. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder -- silent wrongness, which section 4b places outside it rather than at rung 1. ",

    "RUNG AFTER REPAIR: 2, mechanically preventable -- the invalid state stays writable and a per-PR test in compiler_tests refuses both its return and the marker's deletion. ",

    "CEILING: 4, structurally impossible, because the decidable form is to emit NO entry file at all when the corpus declares no entry, at which point the empty-body entry has no constructor and cargo itself refuses the run. ",

    "NEXT TRIGGER: an emitted-population model that admits a crate with no bin target -- the population manifest, the emitted-file census and the harnesses that assemble emitted crates all currently assume src/main.rs is always declared, and that assumption is what holds this class at rung 2 rather than 4. "
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
